# `lm_sensors.service` here and `lm-sensors.service` under `deb/`, matching the
# package rename the manifest already gates: Fedora's `lm_sensors` and the deb
# families' `lm-sensors`. A preset is applied line by line and a unit that does
# not exist fails the build, so one file cannot name both — measured
# 2026-09-05, `Failed to enable unit: Unit lm_sensors.service does not exist`
# on the debian collection leg.
enable lm-sensors.service

# The same on all three: upstream names the unit with an underscore and neither
# archive renames it. Repeated rather than left ungated so each family's preset
# reads as the whole of what this module enables.
enable intel_lpmd.service
